[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 3. Phase 2: Host & Application Hardening
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 2.1: Harden `wp-config.php` Configuration & DB Credentials
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/var/www/html/wp-config.php:4` (`/sas/alerts.json:18`, `/sas/baseline.json:2`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Command:**
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>   cp /var/www/html/wp-config.php /root/forensic_quarantine/20240816_incident/wp-config.php.bak
[?2004l[?2004h>   chmod 0600 /var/www/html/wp-config.php
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Verification:** Verify `/var/www/html/wp-config.php` permissions are `0600`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 2.2: Restrict System Crontab Permissions
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation:** `/disk/etc/crontab:1` (`0644` permissions)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Command:**
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>   chmod 0600 /etc/crontab
[?2004l[?2004h>   chown root:root /etc/crontab
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Verification:** Run `stat -c "%a %U %G" /etc/crontab` (Output must be `600 root root`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 4. Phase 3: Post-Remediation Monitoring
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Log Inspection:** Monitor `/var/log/nginx/access.log` for access attempts to plugin endpoints.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Crontab Audits:** Periodically audit `/var/spool/cron/crontabs/` and `/etc/crontab` for unauthorized tasks.
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Core Verification:** Run `wp core verify-checksums` to confirm WordPress file integrity.
[?2004l[?2004h> """
